  "body": {
    "id": "thm:whole-set-confidence",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "As a corollary of exact projection-and-lift and the compact fixed-matrix formulation, under independent sampling and known randomization, \\(\\Pr_P\\{\\Theta(P)\\subseteq\\mathcal O_n\\}\\geq1-\\alpha\\) for every \\(n\\geq1\\) and every \\(P\\in\\mathcal E_e\\). Membership and every fixed linear support query for \\(\\mathcal O_n\\) reduce to a linear program obtained by adjoining the constraints defining \\(\\mathcal K_n\\) to \\(\\mathcal R(p)\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "P",
      "p",
      "\\Theta(P)",
      "\\mathcal O_n",
      "n",
      "\\alpha",
      "\\mathcal E_e",
      "\\mathcal K_n",
      "\\mathcal R(P)"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:known-randomization",
      "ass:iid-sampling",
      "def:confidence-inversion",
      "thm:tree-projection-lift",
      "thm:compact-formulation"
    ],
    "justification": "The statement covers the entire random identified set in finite samples and remains valid at active-face ties.",
    "gap": "HuangEtAl2017 handles static ordinal bound endpoints and OberReynolds2023 handles scalar transport values; neither gives finite-sample whole-polytope coverage for a longitudinal oracle distribution.",
    "consumer": "SMART-BD can report an honest simultaneous region for every oracle-remission pmf, CDF, quantile, and prespecified linear summary.",
    "proof_tex": "For one cell \\(\\omega\\), put \\(X_i=\\mathbf 1\\{O_i=\\omega\\}\\) and \\(\\mu=P(O=\\omega)\\).  We first derive the required concentration bound.  For any real \\(\\lambda\\),\n\\[\n \\phi_\\mu(\\lambda)\n =\\log E\\exp\\{\\lambda(X_i-\\mu)\\}\n\\]\nsatisfies \\(\\phi_\\mu(0)=\\phi_\\mu'(0)=0\\).  Its second derivative is the variance of a Bernoulli variable under exponential tilting and is at most \\(1/4\\).  Taylor's formula with integral remainder therefore gives \\(\\phi_\\mu(\\lambda)\\leq\\lambda^2/8\\).  Independence and Markov's inequality yield\n\\[\n \\Pr\\{\\widehat p(\\omega)-P(\\omega)\\geq r\\}\n \\leq\\inf_{\\lambda>0}\\exp\\{-\\lambda nr+n\\lambda^2/8\\}\n =e^{-2nr^2};                                             \\tag{32}\n\\]\nthe same calculation with \\(-\\lambda\\) gives the lower tail.  A union bound over \\(|\\Omega|\\) cells and the definition of \\(r_n\\) give\n\\[\n \\Pr_P\\!\\left\\{\\max_{\\omega\\in\\Omega}\n |\\widehat p(\\omega)-P(\\omega)|\\leq r_n\\right\\}\n \\geq1-2|\\Omega|e^{-2nr_n^2}=1-\\alpha.                   \\tag{33}\n\\]\nKnown randomization means \\(P\\in\\mathcal E_e\\).  Thus the event in (33) implies \\(P\\in\\mathcal K_n\\).\n\nOn that event, take any \\(q\\in\\Theta(P)\\).  Exact projection and lift give arrays \\(U,V\\) with \\((q,U,V)\\in\\mathcal R(P)\\).  The definition of \\(\\mathcal O_n\\) permits the witness \\(p=P\\), so \\(q\\in\\mathcal O_n\\).  Since this holds simultaneously for every \\(q\\in\\Theta(P)\\),\n\\[\n \\Pr_P\\{\\Theta(P)\\subseteq\\mathcal O_n\\}\n \\geq\\Pr_P\\{P\\in\\mathcal K_n\\}\\geq1-\\alpha.            \\tag{34}\n\\]\nNo boundary differentiability, active-face uniqueness, or asymptotic limit is used.\n\nFinally, the constraints \\(p\\in\\mathcal E_e\\), the cellwise box constraints defining \\(\\mathcal K_n\\), and the fixed-matrix constraints of \\(\\mathcal R(p)\\) are all linear in the joint variables \\((p,q,U,V)\\).  Fixing \\(q\\) gives one feasibility linear program for membership.  Maximizing \\(c^\\top q\\) gives one linear program for any fixed support query, with the exact primal and dual certificates established in the compact-formulation theorem.",
